          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            This entry discusses the full (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"}> non-perturbative
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum
            data of standard 3d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            (induced from a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            and
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+Chern+class"} second Chern class
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+TQFT"} 3d TQFT
          %p
            (For the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+QFT"} perturbative quantization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Chern-Simons+theory#PerturbativeQuantization"} there
          %p Existing literature knows three sectors of this problem, which overlap but do not coincide
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral+quantization"}> path integral quantization
                \. This may be made precise sense of in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbation theory
                where it involves lots of interesting structure such as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+torsion"} analytic torsion
                (
                %a{:href => "Chern-Simons#theory#Witten89"}> Witten 89
                ). However, being just
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbation theory
                it is just an approximation to the full answer.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
                yields the full (non-perturbative quantization) in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
                1, but does not say anything about codimension 0.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reshetikhin-Turaev+construction"} Reshetikhin-Turaev construction
                produces a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+TQFT"} 3d TQFT
                from algebraic data that is naturally associated with the prequantum data defining Chern-Simons theory (such as the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+energy+representations"} positive energy representations
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+group"} loop group
                of the given
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+group"} quantum group
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "#Sawin06"} Sawin 06
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
          %p The known relation between the second and the third point here is the following:
          %p
            That the complex-geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+functor"} modular functor
            obtained from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of Chern-Simons theory as in (
            %a{:href => "#AxelrodPietraWitten91"}> Axelrod-Pietra-Witten 91
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Hitchin90"} Hitchin 90
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            was shown in (
            %a{:href => "#Laszlo98"}> Laszlo 98
            , see also
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Andersen11"} Andersen 11
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Andersen12"} Andersen 12
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sewing+law"} sewing law
            (and hence really is a modular functor in the strong sense) was shown in (
            %a{:href => "#TsuchiyaUenoYamada"}> Tsuchiya-Ueno-Yamada
            ). By
            %a{:href => "modular%20functor#TopologicalLift"} deprojectivization
            these constructions yield a topological modular functor of the form also obtained from the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reshetikhin-Turaev+construction"} Reshetikhin-Turaev construction
          %p
            These (topological) modular functors are fixed by their
            = succeed "-0" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus"} genus
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AndersenUeno06"} Andersen-Ueno 06
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+tensor+category"} modular tensor category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of 3d Chern-Simons theory to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reshetikhin-Turaev+construction"} Reshetikhin-Turaev construction
            one has to match the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+tensor+categories"} modular tensor categories
            obtained from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            in genus-0 to that associated with the coresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+groups"} quantum groups
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Ostrik14"} Ostrik 14
          %h2#something_more Something more
          %blockquote
            %p random notes, needs to be brought into shape
          %h3#space_of_chernsimons_quantum_states Space of Chern-Simons quantum states
          %p
            Chern-Simons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mi ℏ
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mi CS
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar}S_{CS}) \colon \mathbf{Fields}_{CS} \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}^{n+1} U(1)_{conn}
          %p
            given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
            then choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Sigma}_n
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
            is supposed to naturally induce a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
            on the space of (on-shell) fields over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{Fields}_{CS}(\mathbf{\Sigma}_n)
          %p
            Moreover,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mi ℏ
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar}S)
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}_{CS}(\Sigma)
            is supposed to yield a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+line+bundle"} holomorphic line bundle
            with connection with respect to that complex structure
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mi ℏ
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar}S(\mathbf{\Sigma}_n))
                  \\colon
                  \\mathbf{Fields}_{CS}(\mathbf{\Sigma}_n)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbf{B}U(1)_{conn}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
            of the Chern-Simons theory, already equipped with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+polarization"} Kähler polarization
          %p
            Accordingly, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of the CS action functional assigns to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}_{\mathbf{\Sigma}}
            of holomorphic sections of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mi i
                        %mi ℏ
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Σ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar}S(\mathbf{\Sigma}_n))
          %p
            As the complex structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Sigma}_n
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
            varies over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+complex+structures"} moduli stack of complex structures
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{\Sigma}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Σ
                        %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}_{\mathbf{\Sigma}_n}
            form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            with projective flat connection (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+connection"} Hitchin connection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℋ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi ℳ
                            %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathcal{H}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathcal{M}_{\Sigma}
                  }
          %p The assignment
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma_n \mapsto \mathcal{H}_{\Sigma}
          %p
            natural in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphisms"} diffeomorphisms
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is called the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+functor"} modular functor
            %a{:href => "#ModularFunctorAndEquivariantEllipticCohomology"} below
          %p
            One such section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi
            is to be singled out. For instance if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mi ℏ
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar}S(\Sigma_n))
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+characteristic"} theta characteristic
            then there is up to scale a unique holomorphic section. This singling-out is formalized by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FRS-formalism"} FRS-formalism
          %h3#space_of_wzwmodel_precorrelators Space of WZW-model pre-correlators
          %p
            Under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS3-CFT2+and+CS-WZW+correspondence"} AdS3-CFT2 and CS-WZW correspondence
            the states of Chern-Simons theory also correspond to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+functions"} partition functions
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauged+WZW+model"} gauged WZW model
            and hence to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generating+functions"} generating functions
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlation+functions"} correlation functions
            of the actual
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}(\Sigma_n)
            may also be thought of as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sources"} sources
            of a (higher)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauged+WZW+model"} gauged WZW model
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic principle
            says that the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} quantum state
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavefunction"} wavefunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ψ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Psi \in \Gamma(\mathbf{Fields}_{CS}(\mathbf{\Sigma}_n), L)
          %p
            is also the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generating+function"} generating function
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlators"} correlators
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+derivatives"} functional derivatives
          .un_remark{:style => "border:solid #000000;background: #E6DF13;border-width:2px 1px;padding:0 1em;margin:0 1em;"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mi δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mfrac
                      %mi δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⟨
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi ⋯
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\frac{\delta}{\delta A^{a_1}(z_1)}
                    \\cdots
                    \\frac{\delta}{\delta A^{a_n}(z_n)}
                    \\Psi
                    \=
                    \\left\langle J^{a_1}(z_1) \cdots J^{a_n}(z_n) \right\rangle
          %p
            with respect to the Chern-Simons-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"}> fields
            , hence the WZW
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sources"} sources
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-point+functions"} n-point functions
            of the WZW model for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/current+algebra"} current algebra
            insertions, as indicated
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Gawedzki99"} Gawędzki 99 (4.23), 5.1
          %h3#ModularFunctorAndEquivariantEllipticCohomology Modular functor and equivariant elliptic cohomology
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            (see there at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "equivariant+elliptic+cohomology#InterpretationInQuantumFieldTheory"} interpretation in QFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+functor"} modular functor
            refines from equipping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
            to equipping it with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            it refines from structures of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves"} elliptic curves
            over the complex numbers to general arithmetic elliptic curves (over the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+elliptic+curves"} derived elliptic curves
            (over the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            needs to be refined to admit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarizations"} polarizations
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion+and+idelic+structure"} differential cohesion and idelic structure
            for more on this.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donaldson-Uhlenbeck-Yau+theorem"} Donaldson-Uhlenbeck-Yau theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Narasimhan-Seshadri+theorem"} Narasimhan-Seshadri theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Harder-Narasimhan+theorem"} Harder-Narasimhan theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
          %h2#References References
          %h3#ReferencesNonPerturbative Non-perturbative geometric quantization
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+QFT"} non-perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
          %p Basics are recalled for instance in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Fernando Falceto,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gawedzki"} Krzysztof Gawedzki
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Chern-Simons States at Genus One
                %strong 159
                (1994) 549-580 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9211003"}> arXiv:hep-th/9211003
                )
            %li#Gawedzki99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gawedzki"}> Krzysztof Gawedzki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conformal field theory: a case study
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conformal Field Theory – New Non-perturbative Methods In String And Field Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9904145"} arXiv:hep-th/9904145
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429502873"} doi:10.1201/9780429502873
            %li
              %p
                Yasuhiro Abe,
                %em Application of abelian holonomy formalism to the elementary theory of numbers
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1005.4299"}> arXiv:1005.4299
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of 3d CS theory in codimension 1 is due to:
          %ul
            %li#AxelrodPietraWitten91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scott+Axelrod"}> Scott Axelrod
                , S. Della Pietra,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric quantization of Chern-Simons gauge theory
                %strong 33
                (1991) 787-902 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214446565"}> euclid:jdg/1214446565
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Hitchin90
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nigel+Hitchin"}> Nigel Hitchin
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Flat connections and geometric quantization
                %strong 131
                2 (1990) 347-380 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104200841"}> euclid:cmp/1104200841
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (cf. at
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+connection"} Hitchin connection
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#Atiyah90
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              , Section 5 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Geometry and Physics of Knots
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511623868"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511623868
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://lib.ysu.am/open_books/417997.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+TQFT"} 3d TQFT
            candidate for quantum CS theory in the form of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reshetikhin-Turaev+construction"} Reshetikhin-Turaev construction
            and the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+tensor+category"} modular tensor category
            data is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#ReshetikhinTuraev91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolai+Reshetikhin"}> Nicolai Reshetikhin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Turaev"} Vladimir Turaev
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Invariants of 3-manifolds via link polynomials and quantum groups
                %strong 103
                3 (1991) 547-597 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://mathlab.snu.ac.kr/~top/quantum/article/Reshetikhin01.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#BakalovKirillov
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bojko+Bakalov"}> Bojko Bakalov
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandre+Kirillov"} Alexandre Kirillov
                %em Lectures on tensor categories and modular functors
                AMS, University Lecture Series (2000) (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.sunysb.edu/~kirillov/tensor/tensor.html"}> web
                ).
            %li#Sawin06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Sawin"}> Stephen Sawin
                ,
                %em Quantum groups at roots of unity and modularity
                J. Knot Theory Ramifications
                %strong 15
                10 (2006) 1245-1277 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0308281"}> arXiv:0308281
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Ostrik14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Ostrik"}> Victor Ostrik
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/a/178304/381"} MO comment August 2014
          %p
            The relation between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+functor"} modular functor
            obtained from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            and from geometric quantization of CS theory is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Laszlo98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yves+Laszlo"}> Yves Laszlo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Hitchin’s and WZW connection are the same
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/journals/NYJM/JDG/archive/vol.49/3_5.pdf"} pdf
            %li#TsuchiyaUenoYamada
              %p
                Tsuchiya; K Ueno; Yamada,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conformal field theory on universal family of stable curves with gauge symmetries
            %li#AndersenUeno06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%B8rgen+Andersen"}> Jørgen Andersen
                , K. Ueno,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Modular functors are determined by their genus zero data
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0611087"} arXiv:math/0611087
          %p
            Discussion specific to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} special unitary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%B8rgen+Andersen"}> Jørgen Andersen
                , K. Ueno,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Abelian Conformal Field theories and Determinant Bundles
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%B8rgen+Andersen"}> Jørgen Andersen
                , K. Ueno,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric Construction of Modular Functors from Conformal Field Theory
            %li#Andersen11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%B8rgen+Andersen"}> Jørgen Andersen
                , K. Ueno,
                %em Construction of the Reshetikhin-Turaev TQFT via Conformal Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1110.5027"}> arXiv:1110.5027
                )
            %li#Andersen12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%B8rgen+Andersen"}> Jørgen Andersen
                ,
                %em A geometric formula for the Witten-Reshetikhin-Turaev Quantum Invariants and some applications
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.2785"}> arXiv:1206.2785
                )
          %p For discussion of the state of the proof see also
          %ul
            %li#MODiscussion
              MO,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/86792/why-hasnt-anyone-proved-that-the-two-standard-approaches-to-quantizing-chern-si"} Why hasn’t anyone proved that the two standard approaches to quantizing Chern-Simons theory are equivalent?
          %p
            and in particular
            %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/a/185401/381"} this reply
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Henriques"} Andre Henriques
          %p Detailed review in the case of abelian Chern-Simons theory includes
          %ul
            %li
              Spencer D. Stirling,
              %em Abelian Chern-Simons theory with toral gauge group, modular tensor categories, and group categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0807.2857"}> arXiv:http://arxiv.org/abs/0807.2857v1
              )
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+quantization"} Weyl quantization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+lines"} Wilson lines
            and details on the role of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+functions"} theta functions
            is in
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of Chern-Simons theory
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+quantization"} Weyl quantization
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skein+relations"} skein relations
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%B8rgen+Andersen"}> Jørgen Andersen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation quantization and geometric quantization of abelian moduli spaces
            %li#GelcaUribe02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R%C4%83zvan+Gelca"}> Răzvan Gelca
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alejandro+Uribe"} Alejandro Uribe
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The Weyl quantization and the quantum group quantization of the moduli space of flat
                    = succeed "-connections" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi SU
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                %strong 233
                (2003) 493-512 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0201059"}> arXiv:math-ph/0201059
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#GelcaUribe10b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R%C4%83zvan+Gelca"}> Răzvan Gelca
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alejandro+Uribe"} Alejandro Uribe
                %em
                  Quantum mechanics and non-abelian theta functions for the gauge group
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1007.2010"}> arXiv:1007.2010
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            and for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+Chern-Simons+theory"} abelian Chern-Simons theory
          %ul
            %li#GelcaUribe10a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Razvan+Gelca"}> Razvan Gelca
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alejandro+Uribe"} Alejandro Uribe
              %em From classical theta functions to topological quantum field theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1006.3252"}> arXiv:1006.3252
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ttu.edu/~rgelca/berk.pdf"} slides pdf
          %p Another approach is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"} Mike Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Topological+Quantum+Field+Theories+from+Compact+Lie+Groups#3dCSFullyExtended"} TQFT from compact Lie groups – 3d Chern-Simons as a fully extended TQFT
          %div
            %h3#ReferencesPerturbativeCSTheory Perturbative quantum Chern-Simons theory
            %p
              Discussion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of Chern-Simons theory
              (via
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kontsevich+integrals"} Kontsevich integrals
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knot+graph+cohomology"} knot graph cohomology
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+diagrams"} Jacobi diagrams
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitudes+as+differential+forms+on+configuration+spaces+of+points"} Feynman amplitudes as differential forms on configuration spaces of points
              and yielding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+Vassiliev+invariant"} universal
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vassiliev+invariants"} Vassiliev invariants
            %ul
              %li#BarNatan91
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dror+Bar-Natan"}> Dror Bar-Natan
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Perturbative aspects of the Chern-Simons topological quantum field theory
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/323500"} spire:323500
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://search.proquest.com/docview/303979053"} proquest:303979053
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BarNatanPerturbativeCS91.pdf", :title => ""} BarNatanPerturbativeCS91.pdf
              %li#AxelrodSinger
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scott+Axelrod"}> Scott Axelrod
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Chern-Simons Perturbation Theory
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9110056"} arXiv:hep-th/9110056
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scott+Axelrod"}> Scott Axelrod
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Chern–Simons Perturbation Theory II
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9304087"} arXiv:hep-th/9304087
              %li#Kontsevich93
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Vassiliev’s knot invariants
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://pagesperso.ihes.fr/~maxim/TEXTS/VassilievKnot.pdf"} pdf
              %li#Kontsevich
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Feynman diagrams and low-dimensional topology
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.ihes.fr/~maxim/TEXTS/Feynman%20%20diagrams%20and%20low-dimensional%20topology.pdf"} pdf
              %li#BarNatan95
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dror+Bar-Natan"}> Dror Bar-Natan
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Perturbative Chern-Simons theory
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0218216595000247"} doi:10.1142/S0218216595000247
              %li#AF96
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Altschuler"}> Daniel Altschuler
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laurent+Freidel"} Laurent Freidel
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Vassiliev knot invariants and Chern-Simons perturbation theory to all orders
                  %strong 187
                  (1997) 261-287
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9603010"} arXiv:q-alg/9603010
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s002200050136"} doi:10.1007/s002200050136
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li#LambrechtsVolic14
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pascal+Lambrechts"}> Pascal Lambrechts
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ismar+Voli%C4%87"} Ismar Volić
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Formality of the little N-disks operad
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0808.0457"} arXiv:0808.0457
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/memo/1079"} doi:10.1090/memo/1079
            %p Review:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robbert+Dijkgraaf"}> Robbert Dijkgraaf
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Perturbative topological field theory
                  %em Trieste 1993, Proceedings, String theory, gauge theory and quantum gravity ‘93
                  189-227 (
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/399223/"}> spire:399223
                  ,
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/DijkgraafPerturbativeCS93.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %li#ChmutovDuzhinMostovoy11
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Chmutov"}> Sergei Chmutov
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Duzhin"} Sergei Duzhin
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Mostovoy"} Jacob Mostovoy
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Introduction to Vassiliev knot invariants
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1103.5628"} arxiv/1103.5628
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139107846"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139107846
            %p
              See also at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlator+as+differential+form+on+configuration+space+of+points"} correlator as differential form on configuration space of points
              and see at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+complex"} graph complex
              as a model for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces+of+knots"} spaces of knots
              %em .
            %p
              The “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wheels+theorem"}> Wheels theorem
              ”, saying that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantization+of+3d+Chern-Simons+theory"} perturbative Chern-Simons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loop+observable"} Wilson loop observable
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unknot"} unknot
              is, as a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+Vassiliev+invariant"} universal Vassiliev invariant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/series"} series
              of wheel-shaped
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+diagrams"} Jacobi diagrams
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modified+Bernoulli+numbers"} modified Bernoulli numbers
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dror+Bar-Natan"}> Dror Bar-Natan
                , Thang T Q Le,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dylan+Thurston"} Dylan Thurston
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Two applications of elementary knot theory to Lie algebras and Vassiliev invariants
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.gt/1513883092"} euclid.gt/1513883092
            %p following
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dror+Bar-Natan"}> Dror Bar-Natan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stavros+Garoufalidis"} Stavros Garoufalidis
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lev+Rozansky"} Lev Rozansky
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dylan+Thurston"} Dylan Thurston
                %em Wheels, wheeling, and the Kontsevich integral of the unknot
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9703025"}> q-alg/9703025
                )
        .revisedby
